From 0c56195d343a0df030e2e289a751dfca19dceb29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ecogamezz <33791269+ecogamezz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 05:05:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] WowCraft: Minecraft's HUD on a Retina Mac, and our WoW
 body hidden in third person

- The overlay: Minecraft (SDL) sizes its window in points, so on a Retina Mac the physical size
  we sent it made a 6720 x 4200 frame, which the mod's FrameExporter drops (past 3840 x 2160):
  no HUD ever arrived. On macOS Minecraft now gets our size and the cursor in points, and its
  frame comes out at our pixel size (minecraft_viewport, MINECRAFT_IN_POINTS).
- The overlay swap resets only for a new Minecraft process: a stalled heartbeat (Minecraft
  loading its world) came back to the same process and the reset left both sides on one slot.
- Our WoW body (and a co-op partner's) is hidden after the exterior cull, which set every body
  it admits back to Inherited each frame: in third person the whole WoW character showed
  under the Minecraft body.

Verified: cargo test --release -p benilla-app --no-default-features --lib wowcraft (41),
-p wowcraft-link (8); cargo build --release -p benilla --no-default-features; a live run with
mod/test/CutMinecraft in Minecraft's third-person view: the WoW body, drawn before, is gone,
and the stand-in receives the viewport in points (1280x800 for a 2560x1600 window). The real
Minecraft HUD needs a run with real Minecraft. Built on macOS (Intel) only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
